> The chart gives mild support to the downside: lower highs, price under both averages, and a failed hold of $141.79. A daily close above $149.13 would flip that. A daily close under $135 points to $120.39. The chart disagrees with management. The company describes accelerating revenue and a compute shortage; the stock is 38% under its June high and has spent 22 of its 106 sessions closing below the IPO price.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>Q4 results (date not announced; one site forecasts Feb 9, 2027): whether capex landed in $35–40B and revenue is on track for $33–37B in Q1.</li><li>Any terms from the Tesla special committees, and how outside holders are treated in them.</li><li>Texas after Jan 19, and how the new compute is paid for (more debt, or cash).</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>High on reported figures and on the Q4 capex and Q1 revenue ranges (company transcript, read twice in the source research). Medium on Starship and compute timelines. Governance percentages come from a secondary write-up of the prospectus, not the filing itself; the prospectus was not opened. Left out as unverified: a reported monthly compute contract with a named customer, and a reported remark that Q4 revenue would rise about 70%. Political and market claims are as reported by TheStreet.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://s21.q4cdn.com/184289198/files/content_files/SpaceX-Third-Quarter-2026-Webcast-Transcript.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Company call transcript (PDF)</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001181412/000162828026066880/spcx-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-Q</a> · <a href=\"https://pulse2.com/spacex-q3-revenue-surges-161-to-14-6-billion-as-super-intelligence-and-starlink-growth-accelerate/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Results recap</a> · <a href=\"https://www.constellationr.com/insights/news/spacexs-q3-musk-says-it-could-rent-out-its-ai-compute-several-times-over\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Constellation Research</a> · <a href=\"https://investinglive.com/stocks/spacex-beats-q3-forecasts-across-all-three-segments-as-ai-revenue-tops-7-5-billion/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">investingLive</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.rte.ie/news/business/2026/0421/1569379-musk-insiders-to-keep-voting-control-of-spacex-after-ipo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">RTÉ on voting control</a> · <a href=\"https://www.softwareseni.com/what-spacex-public-shareholders-actually-get-and-why-institutional-investors-objected\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SoftwareSeni on shareholder rights</a> · <a href=\"https://vestedfinance.com/blog/us-stocks/inside-spacexs-s-1-decoding-the-three-engine-bet-going-public-as-spcx/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Prospectus coverage</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.aol.com/articles/spacex-investors-confront-painful-post-010700000.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TheStreet via AOL, Nov 12</a> · <a href=\"https://www.texastribune.org/2026/11/04/data-center-texas-pause-gina-hinojosa-governor-policies/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Texas Tribune on the data center pause</a> · <a href=\"https://www.space.com/space-exploration/launches-spacecraft/spacex-will-launch-epic-double-catch-starship-flight-15-test-mission-on-nov-13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Space.com on Starship Flight 15</a></li></ul>"}